---
import DemoStatus from '../components/DemoStatus.astro'
import Next from '../components/Next.astro'
import Snippet from '../components/Snippet.astro'
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro'
---

<Page
  page="document"
  title="Document"
  description="The same requests are your API docs, on your own site: notes beside each operation, your branding, and a Try it button that runs in place."
>
  <section class="hero" style="padding-bottom: 24px">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="eyebrow">03 · Document</span>
      <h1 class="display">Docs that run.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        The requests you wrote are the examples. Put them in your own docs site and every one gets a Try it
        that sends a real request, in a panel over your page, in your theme.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block" style="padding-top: 8px">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 class="title">Mark what should run</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          One script and a data attribute. A plain element gets a Play button beside it; a button or link that
          carries the attribute opens the panel itself.
        </p>
      </div>
      <Snippet file="snippets/embed.html" region="embed" title="docs.html" />

      <div class="demo">
        <div class="demo-bar">
          <span class="dots" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span>
          <span>On this page, it does this</span>
          <span class="grow"></span>
          <DemoStatus reset={false} />
        </div>
        <div class="demo-body prose" style="max-width: none">
          <p data-specbook-try="petstore/GetPetById" data-specbook-env="demo">
            Fetch a pet by its id, and see the response checked against the spec.
          </p>
          <p>
            <button type="button" data-specbook-flow="new-pet" data-specbook-env="demo">
              Register a pet with a generated name
            </button>
            , or
            <button
              type="button"
              data-specbook-flow="adopt-pet"
              data-specbook-env="demo"
              data-specbook-inputs='{"quantity":2}'
            >
              adopt two
            </button>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2 class="title">It looks like your site</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          The panel is isolated from your page, so your styles cannot break it and it cannot break yours. It
          wears your colors, follows your light or dark theme as it changes, and keeps what a visitor types out of
          your storage.
        </p>
      </div>
      <Snippet file="snippets/theme.css" region="theme" title="site.css" />

      <h2 class="title">Notes beside the operations</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Markdown next to what it describes becomes the documentation: <code>sequences/&lt;name&gt;.seq.md</code>
          for a flow, <code>requests/&lt;service&gt;/&lt;Operation&gt;/README.md</code> for an operation. A heading
          made of one code span, like <code>## `status`</code>, attaches the text under it to that field. The
          <a href="/reference/embed/">reference</a> has the details.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="wrap"><Next page="document" /></div>
</Page>
